The Following is a list of ToolTypes for this ICON:


NOTICE: ALL TOOLTYPES ARE CASE SENSITIVE

ABOUT: This ICON defines a MODULE for /X.

       This ICON may be in the following directories:

         a> BBSCmd     - Modules in this directory are allowed to be
                         executed from any menu prompt or MCI text file.

         b> SysCmd     - Modules in this directory are only accessible by
                         MCI text files and internal BBS operations.

         c> Conf(x)Cmd - Modules in this directory are allowed to be 
                         executed from conference (x) menu prompt or from
                         any MCI text file in conference (x).


LOCATION=
MULTINODE=
ACCESS=
TYPE=
STACK=
PASSWORD=


LOCATION=<string>

         -Version 3.0
         -REQUIRED
         -Specifies the location of the Module.
         -If the location is a directory, then the directory name must have
          a trailing '/'.

     LOCATION=DOORS:Module/


MULTINODE=<YES|NO>

         -Version 3.0
         -REQUIRED
         -tells /X if the module may be simultaniously accessed from other nodes.

     MULTINODE=YES
     MULTINODE=NO


ACCESS=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -REQUIRED
         -tells /X the access level required to run this module.
         -This option is ignored for internal Module options.

     ACCESS=200


TYPE=<XIM | AIM | TIM | IIM>

         -Version 3.0
         -REQUIRED
         -tells /X which type of module it is to support:

          XIM =/X Standard Module.
          AIM =Arexx Module (requires REXXDOOR in the BBS:Utils directory)
          TIM =Traditional BBS Module (requires PARADOOR) in the BBS:Utils
                directory)
          IIM =NO INTERFACE - This type of Module will SPAWN the specified
                MODULE and not wait on it to finish.

     TYPE=XIM


STACK=<num>

         -Version 3.0
         -OPTIONAL
         -tells /X the stacksize to use when launching this module.
         -Default is 4096.

     STACK=60000


PASSWORD=<string>

         -Version 3.0 (reserved for future implementation)
         -OPTIONAL
         -makes the user enter a password before executing this module.

     PASSWORD=PIGME


